@* Products.razor — Phase 3.1
   Customer-facing product catalog at route `/Products`. All authenticated
   users can browse here. Customers land here directly after login (per
   roadmap Section 12.8). Staff users arrive here from the sidebar's
   "Products" link.

   LAYOUT:
     1. Page header: title + (optional, staff-only) "Manage Products" link
        to /Admin/Products.
     2. Filter bar: search box + category dropdown + stock-status filter.
     3. Product card grid: responsive (1 col mobile, 2 col tablet, 3-4 col
        desktop) using RadzenRow + RadzenColumn. Each card shows picture
        placeholder, name, price, stock badge, and a "View details" button.
     4. Pager: simple prev/next + page count display.
     5. Empty state when no products match the filters.

   DATA LOADING:
     - OnInitializedAsync: load the user's roles + active categories (for
       the filter dropdown) + the first page of products.
     - On filter/page change: re-call GetProductsPaginatedQuery via
       Wolverine. Server-side paging (PageSize=12 — 4 cols × 3 rows on
       desktop, scales down on mobile).
     - Search is debounced via RadzenTextBox's `Change` EventCallback
       (fires on Enter or blur, NOT on every keystroke — that would
       hammer the bus).

   CART INTEGRATION (DEFERRED):
     The "Add to cart" button on each card is intentionally NOT in this
     page. Per roadmap Section 12.4, the add-to-cart flow needs
     `GetActiveDraftForUserAsync` on ISaleRepository (which doesn't exist
     yet) plus a CreateOrAppendSale command wrapper. That infrastructure
     lands with Phase 4.1 (Cart page). For Phase 3.1, the catalog is a
     browse-and-discover surface — clicking a card navigates to
     /Products/{Id} (Phase 3.2, also not built yet) for full details.

   ROLE-AWARE BEHAVIOR:
     - All authenticated users can browse.
     - "Manage Products" link in header: staff only (Admin/Manager/Employee)
       — hidden for Customer/ReadOnly per Section 12.1.
     - Stock filter has 3 values: All / In Stock / Out of Stock. Applied
       client-side on the loaded page (cheap — the page already has 12 items).

   LOCALIZATION:
     All user-visible strings go through IStringLocalizer<Products> (Loc).
     Numbers (price, stock) are formatted with the current culture's
     NumberFormatInfo — Persian shows Persian digits when the culture is
     fa-IR (handled automatically by Blazor's @CultureInfo logic).

   ANTIFORGERY:
     Not needed here — no EditForm, no POST. Pure read-only browsing
     surface (filter changes trigger a new GET via Wolverine query, not a
     form POST). *@

@page "/Products"
@attribute [Authorize]
@using System.Globalization
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using Wolverine
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Authorization
@using TakOne.Application.Common.Interfaces
@using TakOne.Application.Products.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Products.Queries.GetProductsPaginated
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.DTOs
@using TakOne.Application.Categories.Queries.GetActiveCategories
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.Common
@using TakOne.SharedKernel.DTOs
@inject IMessageBus MessageBus
@inject ICurrentUserService CurrentUser
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@inject IStringLocalizer<Products> Loc

<PageTitle>@Loc["PageTitle"]</PageTitle>

<HeadContent>
    <style>
            /* Product card — uniform height across the row so the grid looks
                       tidy even when product names wrap to 2 lines. Hover effect gives
                       affordance that the card is clickable. */
            .product-card {
                transition: transform 0.18s ease, box-shadow 0.18s ease;
                cursor: pointer;
                height: 100%;
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
            }

                .product-card:hover {
                    transform: translateY(-2px);
                    box-shadow: 0 8px 16px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
                }

            /* Picture placeholder — when the product has no PictureUrl, we show
                       a Material icon centered on a neutral background. Same aspect
                       ratio across cards keeps the grid tidy. */
            .product-picture {
                aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
                display: flex;
                align-items: center;
                justify-content: center;
                background: var(--rz-base-background-color);
                border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rz-base-border-color);
                overflow: hidden;
            }

                .product-picture img {
                    width: 100%;
                    height: 100%;
                    object-fit: contain;
                }

                .product-picture .rz-icon {
                    font-size: 4rem;
                    color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);
                }

            /* Card body pushes the action button to the bottom via flex.
                       Equal-height rows make the grid look clean. */
            .product-card .rz-card-body {
                display: flex;
                flex-direction: column;
                flex: 1;
                gap: 0.5rem;
            }

            .product-name {
                font-weight: 600;
                font-size: 1rem;
                line-height: 1.3;
                /* Clamp to 2 lines so long names don't blow up the card */
                display: -webkit-box;
                -webkit-line-clamp: 2;
                -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
                overflow: hidden;
            }

            .product-price {
                font-size: 1.1rem;
                font-weight: 700;
                color: var(--rz-primary);
            }

            .product-stock {
                font-size: 0.85rem;
            }

            .product-stock-low {
                color: var(--rz-warning);
            }

            .product-stock-out {
                color: var(--rz-danger);
            }
    </style>
</HeadContent>

<RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Vertical" Gap="1rem">
    @* ── Page header ──
       Title + (staff-only) "Manage Products" link to /Admin/Products.
       Per Section 12.7 (hide, don't disable), the link is wrapped in
       AuthorizeView and simply absent for Customer/ReadOnly users. *@
    <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal"
                 AlignItems="AlignItems.Center"
                 JustifyContent="JustifyContent.SpaceBetween">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal" AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.75rem">
            <RadzenIcon Icon="inventory_2" Style="font-size: 1.75rem; color: var(--rz-primary);" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["PageHeading"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H5" Style="font-weight: 600; margin: 0;" />
        </RadzenStack>

        <AuthorizeView Roles="@(Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Manager + "," + Roles.Employee)">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ManageProductsButton"]"
                          Icon="settings"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@(() => Navigation.NavigateTo("/Admin/Products", forceLoad: false))" />
        </AuthorizeView>
    </RadzenStack>

    @* ── Filter bar ──
       Three controls in a row, wrap on mobile. Each control re-triggers
       LoadProductsAsync() via its respective callback. *@
    <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 1rem;">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal"
                     AlignItems="AlignItems.End"
                     JustifyContent="JustifyContent.SpaceBetween"
                     Wrap="FlexWrap.Wrap"
                     Gap="1rem">
            @* Search box — fires OnSearch on Enter or blur (NOT every keystroke).
               `@bind-Value` with the default binding event (onchange) updates
               `_searchTerm` when the user presses Enter or leaves the field.
               `@bind-Value:after` then fires our handler AFTER the value is
               updated, so `LoadProductsAsync` sees the new value. This is the
               Blazor 7+ idiomatic pattern for "react to a committed value
               change" — much simpler than wiring `ValueChanged` + manual
               state-assignment, and avoids firing on every keystroke. *@
            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["SearchLabel"]" Style="flex: 1 1 240px; min-width: 200px;">
                <RadzenTextBox @bind-Value="_searchTerm"
                               @bind-Value:after="OnSearchChanged"
                               Placeholder="@Loc["SearchPlaceholder"]"
                               TValue="string" />
            </RadzenFormField>

            @* Category dropdown — populated from GetActiveCategoriesQuery.
               "All categories" is the default (null selection).
               NOTE on AllowClear: this is a real RadzenDropDown parameter
               in v11.1.1 (verified via ERP reference SalesList.razor line 106). *@
            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["CategoryLabel"]" Style="flex: 0 1 220px; min-width: 180px;">
                <RadzenDropDown Value="_selectedCategoryId"
                                Data="_categories"
                                TValue="Guid?"
                                TextProperty="Name"
                                ValueProperty="Id"
                                AllowClear="true"
                                Placeholder="@Loc["AllCategories"]"
                                ValueChanged="@OnCategoryChanged"
                                Style="width: 100%;" />
            </RadzenFormField>

            @* Stock-status filter — client-side filter on the loaded page.
               Three options: All / In Stock / Out of Stock. We don't push
               this to the backend (the GetProductsPaginatedQuery doesn't
               accept it). Filtering happens in the @foreach projection. *@
            <RadzenFormField Text="@Loc["StockLabel"]" Style="flex: 0 1 180px; min-width: 140px;">
                <RadzenDropDown Value="_stockFilter"
                                Data="_stockFilterOptions"
                                TValue="StockFilter"
                                TextProperty="Label"
                                ValueProperty="Value"
                                ValueChanged="@OnStockFilterChanged"
                                Style="width: 100%;" />
            </RadzenFormField>
        </RadzenStack>
    </RadzenCard>

    @* ── Loading spinner ── *@
    @if (_isLoading)
    {
        <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center"
                     Style="height: 40vh;" Gap="1rem">
            <RadzenProgressBarCircular ShowValue="false"
                                       Mode="ProgressBarMode.Indeterminate"
                                       Size="ProgressBarCircularSize.Large" />
            <RadzenText Text="@Loc["LoadingText"]"
                        TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                        Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
        </RadzenStack>
    }

    @* ── Error banner ── *@
    else if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(_loadError))
    {
        <RadzenAlert Title="@Loc["ErrorTitle"]"
                     Text="@_loadError"
                     AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Danger"
                     Variant="Variant.Filled"
                     ShowIcon="true">
            <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["RetryButton"]"
                          Icon="refresh"
                          ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                          Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                          Click="@LoadProductsAsync"
                          Style="margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
        </RadzenAlert>
    }

    @* ── Empty state ── *@
    else if (_filteredProducts.Count == 0)
    {
        <RadzenCard Variant="Variant.Filled" Style="padding: 3rem; text-align: center;">
            <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="1rem">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="search_off" Style="font-size: 3rem; color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color);" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["EmptyTitle"]" TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" />
                <RadzenText Text="@Loc["EmptyMessage"]"
                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); max-width: 360px;" />
                <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ClearFiltersButton"]"
                              Icon="filter_alt_off"
                              ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Secondary"
                              Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                              Click="@ClearFilters" />
            </RadzenStack>
        </RadzenCard>
    }

    @* ── Product card grid ── *@
    else
    {
        <RadzenRow Gap="1rem">
            @foreach (var product in _filteredProducts)
            {
                <RadzenColumn Size="12" SizeMD="6" SizeLG="4" SizeXL="3">
                    <RadzenCard class="product-card" Variant="Variant.Filled">
                        @* Picture — if PictureUrl is null, show a placeholder icon.
                           The whole card is clickable, so we navigate on click. *@
                        <div class="product-picture" @onclick="@(() => GoToProductDetail(product.Id))">
                            @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(product.PictureUrl))
                            {
                                <img src="@product.PictureUrl" alt="@product.Name" loading="lazy" />
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="image" />
                            }
                        </div>

                        <RadzenStack Gap="0.5rem" Style="flex: 1;">
                            <div class="product-name" @onclick="@(() => GoToProductDetail(product.Id))">
                                @product.Name
                            </div>

                            <div class="product-price">
                                @FormatPrice(product.Price)
                            </div>

                            <div class="product-stock @GetStockClass(product.StockQuantity)">
                                <RadzenIcon Icon="@GetStockIcon(product.StockQuantity)"
                                            Style="font-size: 0.95rem; vertical-align: middle;" />
                                <span style="vertical-align: middle; margin-left: 0.25rem;">
                                    @GetStockLabel(product.StockQuantity)
                                </span>
                            </div>
                        </RadzenStack>

                        @* "View details" button — full-width, primary action.
                           The whole card is also clickable, but a visible button
                           gives better affordance for touch users (the card click
                           target can be hard to discover on mobile). *@
                        <RadzenButton Text="@Loc["ViewDetailsButton"]"
                                      Icon="arrow_forward"
                                      ButtonStyle="ButtonStyle.Primary"
                                      Variant="Variant.Outlined"
                                      Click="@(() => GoToProductDetail(product.Id))"
                                      Style="width: 100%; margin-top: 0.5rem;" />
                    </RadzenCard>
                </RadzenColumn>
            }
        </RadzenRow>

        @* ── Pager ──
           Manual pager (Prev / page numbers / Next) rather than RadzenDataPager
           — RadzenDataPager IS a real Radzen component, but the ERP reference
           project doesn't use it (they use RadzenDataGrid's built-in pager
           for tables). For our card-grid catalog, a manual pager is simpler
           and removes any API uncertainty. The pager operates on the
           PaginatedResult metadata from the backend (true server-side paging). *@
        @if (_totalCount > _pageSize)
        {
            <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal"
                         JustifyContent="JustifyContent.Center"
                         AlignItems="AlignItems.Center"
                         Gap="0.5rem"
                         Wrap="FlexWrap.Wrap"
                         Style="margin-top: 1rem;">
                <RadzenButton Icon="chevron_left"
                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                              Disabled="@(_pageNumber <= 1)"
                              Click="@(() => OnPageChanged(_pageNumber - 1))" />

                @{
                    var totalPages = (int)Math.Ceiling((double)_totalCount / _pageSize);
                    var startPage = Math.Max(1, _pageNumber - 2);
                    var endPage = Math.Min(totalPages, startPage + 4);
                    if (endPage - startPage < 4) startPage = Math.Max(1, endPage - 4);
                }

                @for (var p = startPage; p <= endPage; p++)
                {
                    var page = p; // closure capture for the lambda
                                  <RadzenButton Text="@(page.ToString())"
                                                Variant="@(page == _pageNumber ? Variant.Filled : Variant.Text)"
                                                ButtonStyle="@(page == _pageNumber ? ButtonStyle.Primary : ButtonStyle.Base)"
                                                Disabled="@(_isLoading)"
                                                Click="@(() => OnPageChanged(page))" />
                }

                <RadzenButton Icon="chevron_right"
                              Variant="Variant.Text"
                              Disabled="@(_pageNumber >= Math.Ceiling((double)_totalCount / _pageSize))"
                              Click="@(() => OnPageChanged(_pageNumber + 1))" />

                <RadzenText Text="@string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["PageInfoFormat"], _pageNumber, totalPages, _totalCount)"
                            TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption"
                            Style="color: var(--rz-text-secondary-color); margin-left: 0.5rem;" />
            </RadzenStack>
        }
    }
</RadzenStack>

@code {
    // ── State ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// The full page of products returned by the backend (BEFORE the
    /// client-side stock filter is applied). We keep this around so that
    /// toggling the stock filter doesn't require a round-trip.
    /// </summary>
    private List<ProductListItemDto> _products = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// The products actually rendered — _products filtered by _stockFilter.
    /// Computed once per render cycle.
    /// </summary>
    private List<ProductListItemDto> _filteredProducts => _stockFilter switch
    {
        StockFilter.InStock => _products.Where(p => p.StockQuantity > 0).ToList(),
        StockFilter.OutOfStock => _products.Where(p => p.StockQuantity == 0).ToList(),
        _ => _products
    };

    private List<CategoryDto> _categories = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// Filter state. All start empty/null (= "show everything").
    /// </summary>
    private string _searchTerm = string.Empty;
    private Guid? _selectedCategoryId;
    private StockFilter _stockFilter = StockFilter.All;

    /// <summary>
    /// Pager state. _pageSize=12 gives 4×3 on desktop, 2×6 on tablet,
    /// 1×12 on mobile — all clean layouts with the RadzenColumn sizes
    /// declared in the markup.
    /// </summary>
    private const int _pageSize = 12;
    private int _pageNumber = 1;
    private int _totalCount;

    /// <summary>
    /// Loading/error state.
    /// </summary>
    private bool _isLoading = true;
    private string _loadError = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>
    /// The dropdown options for the stock-status filter. Built once on init.
    /// Each entry is (Value, Label) — the Label is localized at render time
    /// so the dropdown reflects the current culture.
    /// </summary>
    private List<StockFilterOption> _stockFilterOptions = new();

    /// <summary>
    /// Simple DTO for the dropdown options. Using a class (not a tuple)
    /// because RadzenDropDown's TextProperty/ValueProperty use reflection.
    /// </summary>
    private sealed class StockFilterOption
    {
        public StockFilter Value { get; init; }
        public string Label { get; init; } = string.Empty;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// The stock-status filter values.
    /// </summary>
    private enum StockFilter
    {
        All,
        InStock,
        OutOfStock
    }

    // ── Lifecycle ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        // Build the stock-filter dropdown options. The labels are localized
        // at this point — they won't update if the user switches language
        // mid-session, but that's an acceptable tradeoff (the culture switch
        // force-loads the page, which re-runs OnInitializedAsync anyway).
        _stockFilterOptions = new List<StockFilterOption>
        {
            new() { Value = StockFilter.All, Label = Loc["StockAll"] },
            new() { Value = StockFilter.InStock, Label = Loc["StockInStock"] },
            new() { Value = StockFilter.OutOfStock, Label = Loc["StockOutOfStock"] }
        };

        // Read the ?category=... query param if present (e.g. when the user
        // navigates here from the Categories tree page in a future phase).
        // We use NavigationManager.Uri + System.Web.HttpUtility to parse
        // — Blazor's [SupplyParameterFromQuery] only works on component
        // parameters, and we'd rather not pollute the parameter surface
        // for a one-shot optional seed.
        var uri = Navigation.ToAbsoluteUri(Navigation.Uri);
        if (System.Web.HttpUtility.ParseQueryString(uri.Query)["category"] is { } catIdStr
            && Guid.TryParse(catIdStr, out var catId))
        {
            _selectedCategoryId = catId;
        }

        try
        {
            // Load categories + first page of products in parallel. The two
            // queries are independent — running them concurrently saves a
            // round-trip on initial page load.
            await Task.WhenAll(
                LoadCategoriesAsync(),
                LoadProductsAsync());
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Data loading ────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task LoadCategoriesAsync()
    {
        try
        {
            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<Result<List<CategoryDto>>>(
                new GetActiveCategoriesQuery());

            if (result.IsSuccess)
            {
                _categories = result.Value;
            }
            // Non-fatal: if categories fail to load, the dropdown will just
            // be empty. The user can still browse all products.
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            // Swallow — categories are an optional filter, not the main content.
            // If they don't load, the user can still search + browse.
        }
    }

    private async Task LoadProductsAsync()
    {
        _isLoading = true;
        _loadError = string.Empty;

        try
        {
            var query = new GetProductsPaginatedQuery
            {
                PageNumber = _pageNumber,
                PageSize = _pageSize,
                SearchTerm = string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(_searchTerm) ? null : _searchTerm.Trim(),
                CategoryId = _selectedCategoryId
            };

            var result = await MessageBus.InvokeAsync<PaginatedResult<ProductListItemDto>>(query);

            _products = result.Items.ToList();
            _totalCount = result.TotalCount;

            // If the page is now empty (e.g. user filtered down to nothing),
            // bump the page number back to 1 and retry. Common case: user
            // was on page 5, then applied a filter that only has 2 pages —
            // we don't want to leave them stranded on an empty page 5.
            if (_products.Count == 0 && _pageNumber > 1)
            {
                _pageNumber = 1;
                await LoadProductsAsync();
                return;
            }
        }
        catch (Exception)
        {
            _loadError = Loc["Error_FailedToLoad"];
        }
        finally
        {
            _isLoading = false;
        }
    }

    // ── Filter change handlers ──────────────────────────────────────────

    private async Task OnSearchChanged()
    {
        // `_searchTerm` has already been updated by @bind-Value before this
        // handler fires (that's what :after means). We just need to reset
        // the page and re-load.
        _pageNumber = 1;
        await LoadProductsAsync();
    }

    private async Task OnCategoryChanged(Guid? categoryId)
    {
        _selectedCategoryId = categoryId;
        _pageNumber = 1;
        await LoadProductsAsync();
    }

    private Task OnStockFilterChanged(StockFilter filter)
    {
        // Stock filter is CLIENT-SIDE — no backend call needed. We just
        // update the state and let the @foreach projection re-compute.
        _stockFilter = filter;
        return Task.CompletedTask;
    }

    private async Task OnPageChanged(int newPage)
    {
        _pageNumber = newPage;
        await LoadProductsAsync();
    }

    private async Task ClearFilters()
    {
        _searchTerm = string.Empty;
        _selectedCategoryId = null;
        _stockFilter = StockFilter.All;
        _pageNumber = 1;
        await LoadProductsAsync();
    }

    // ── Navigation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    private void GoToProductDetail(Guid productId)
    {
        // Phase 3.2 will build /Products/{Id}. For now, navigating there
        // will 404 — but the route is reserved and the URL is meaningful
        // (users can copy/paste it). Once 3.2 lands, this just works.
        Navigation.NavigateTo($"/Products/{productId}", forceLoad: false);
    }

    // ── Display helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// <summary>
    /// Formats a MoneyDto for display: amount in current culture + currency
    /// code. Persian culture shows Persian digits + RTL; English shows
    /// Latin digits + LTR. The currency code is shown as-is (e.g. "IRR"
    /// or "USD") — we don't localize the currency symbol because TakOne
    /// hasn't decided on the currency yet (roadmap open question #2).
    /// </summary>
    private static string FormatPrice(MoneyDto price)
    {
        if (price is null) return "—";
        return $"{price.Amount.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.CurrentCulture)} {price.Currency}";
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns "out", "low", or "" based on stock level. Used by the
    /// CSS class on the stock indicator to color it (red/orange/default).
    /// Threshold for "low" is 10 units — configurable here in one place
    /// if we want to tune it later.
    /// </summary>
    private static string GetStockClass(int stock)
    {
        if (stock == 0) return "product-stock-out";
        if (stock <= 10) return "product-stock-low";
        return string.Empty;
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns a Material icon name for the stock indicator.
    /// - In stock → "check_circle" (green-ish via CSS class)
    /// - Low stock → "warning" (orange)
    /// - Out of stock → "cancel" (red)
    /// </summary>
    private static string GetStockIcon(int stock)
    {
        if (stock == 0) return "cancel";
        if (stock <= 10) return "warning";
        return "check_circle";
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Returns a localized stock label: "In stock (N)", "Low stock (N)",
    /// or "Out of stock". Uses Loc[] so the strings come from the resx
    /// files. The number is interpolated with the current culture's
    /// digit formatting (Persian digits in fa-IR, Latin in en-US).
    /// </summary>
    private string GetStockLabel(int stock)
    {
        if (stock == 0) return Loc["StockOut"];
        if (stock <= 10) return string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["StockLowFormat"], stock);
        return string.Format(CultureInfo.CurrentCulture, Loc["StockInFormat"], stock);
    }
}